    ["……项链我不卖了，你还给我吧。"] = "...I'm not selling the necklace anymore, give it back to me.",
    ["　　第一轮：黛丝不是前来占卜的顾客，<InvHighlight>是一位占卜师</>。\n　　第二轮：黛丝并非死于割伤，而<InvHighlight>是死于法阵</>。 \n　　第三轮：黛丝的死和邪恶仪式无关，<InvHighlight>和她的占卜有关</>。\n　　第四轮：黛丝的死与反锁的占卜室无关，而<InvHighlight>与占卜的结果、前来占卜的顾客有关</>。\n\n　　桌面的线索：一本《仪式魔法：向神明祈求之术》，有两页被折了角，分别是《假死与复生》和《命运的交换》，分别记载着<InvHighlight>不同的仪式魔法内容</>。"] = "Round 1: Daisy was not a customer who came for divination, <InvHighlight> but a diviner. </> \n Round 2: Daisy did not die from the cut, but <InvHighlight> died from the magic circle. </> \n Round 3: Daisy's death has nothing to do with an evil ritual, <InvHighlight> but with her divination. </> \n Round 4: Daisy's death has nothing to do with the locked divination room, but <InvHighlight> with the result of the divination and the customer who came for it. </> \n \n Clues on the table: A book \"Ritual Magic: The Art of Praying to Gods,\" with two pages dog-eared, namely \"Feigned Death and Resurrection\" and \"Exchange of Fate,\" which record <InvHighlight> different ritual magic contents. </>",
    ["　　药量还是老样子，每日一次，禁止加量。上周你私自加量的事，不要再有第二次。\n　　心悸的频率没有下降，这是我目前最担心的，再这样下去，你的心脏撑不了多久了。\n       如果下次又半夜发作，别硬扛，不管几点，都要让约翰先生来找我。\n       霍克斯先生，我是你的医生，观察你是我的本分，这不是监视！如果你连我都开始怀疑，那恰恰说明，那东西对你的影响比我想的还要深，这让我很不安。\n　　下周四下午三点，我会准时到。希望那个时候，你还是我认识的那个霍克斯先生。"] = "    The dosage is the same as before, once a day, increasing the dose is prohibited. Do not let the incident where you increased the dose without permission last week happen a second time. \n    The frequency of palpitations has not decreased, which is my biggest concern right now. If this continues, your heart won't last much longer. \n    If it happens again in the middle of the night, don't try to tough it out. No matter what time it is, have Mr. John come find me. \n    Mr. Hawks, I am your doctor, observing you is my duty, this is not surveillance! If you have started to doubt even me, that precisely shows that the thing has a deeper influence on you than I thought, which makes me very uneasy. \n    Next Thursday at 3 PM, I will arrive on time. I hope that by then, you are still the Mr. Hawks I know.",
